{
  "_comment": [
    "What radiusd's service identity is granted, and nothing else is.",
    "",
    "The peios.auth.authenticate capability lets it ask authd to verify a",
    "password or an MSCHAPv2 response. It is not given peios.auth.logon:",
    "radiusd creates no token and no logon session. authd's default",
    "AuthenticationSecurity already grants radiusd ReadGroups and ReadClaim,",
    "which admission reads; an explicit AuthenticationSecurity replaces that",
    "default, and must then grant them itself.",
    "",
    "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege lets it traverse directories, and",
    "SeAuditPrivilege lets it write its events (radiusd.evman) and the",
    "kernel's audit of its access checks.",
    "",
    "authd unions the privileges of every SID on a token, and a service",
    "token carries the S-1-5-80 service SID derived from the service name,",
    "so a record named for that SID grants these to the one service. The SID",
    "is SHA-1 of 'RADIUSD' as upper-cased UTF-16LE, read as five",
    "little-endian u32s (authd/src/service_sid.rs), radius-management's",
    "SERVICE_SID, which its tests check it against.",
    "",
    "Separate from radiusd-service.reg because a grant is a different kind",
    "of statement from a service definition: an image may review or withhold",
    "it.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the radius package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy\\S-1-5-80-1653768611-2164381495-1902105107-3452022516-881820819",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Capabilities", "type": "multi", "data": ["peios.auth.authenticate"] },
        {
          "name": "Privileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeChangeNotifyPrivilege", "SeAuditPrivilege"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
